DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       AAmmdd is a daemon that automatically mounts filesystems whenever  a  file
       or directory within that filesystem is accessed.  Filesystems are auto‐
       matically unmounted when they appear to have become quiescent.

       AAmmdd operates by attaching itself as an NFS server to each of the speci‐
       fied _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_i_e_s..  Lookups within the specified directories are handled
       by  aammdd,  which uses the map defined by _m_a_p_n_a_m_e to determine how to re‐
       solve the lookup.  Generally, this will be a host name, some filesystem
       information and some mount options for the given filesystem.

       In the first form depicted above, aammdd will print a short  help  string.
       In the second form, if no options are specified, or the ‐‐FF is used, aammdd
       will  read  configuration  parameters from the file _c_o_n_f___f_i_l_e which de‐
       faults to //eettcc//aammdd..ccoonnff.  The last form is described below.

